IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g5-nouns.l4: the nouns of group G5 (Articles 13 and 14 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014) that domain.l4 does not hold.
-- DECLARE and nothing else: no rules and no #EVAL.  Every rule module of the group (g5-art13-effects, g5-art13-reporting,
-- g5-art14-court-powers) imports this file, so that a record is declared once.  Every noun here is a fact a witness could
-- testify to ("the proposal has been made"), the party or act of a regulative rule, or one of the enumerations a rule reads.
-- A judgement of the Commissioner, the Minister or the court ("to the satisfaction of", "appears to the court", "inconsistent
-- with") is a Boolean field named for what is judged; the encoding records that it was judged, it does not judge.
-- The forks of the group are not here but in g5-interpretation.

§ `Charities (Jersey) Law 2014`

§§ `Part 4 -- Charity register: nouns of Article 13 (Effects of registration)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The acts of Article 13, by what is done (not by the Article that requires it).
-- The performer of each is the PARTY of the rule that uses it: a registered charity, the Commissioner, the Minister or the States.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Subject of an Order under Article 13` IS ONE OF
    `a further matter that a registered charity must promptly report, Article 13(6)(h)`
    `a further matter that an annual return must contain, Article 13(7)`
    `the format and timing of the annual return, Article 13(8)`
    `the consequences of lateness of the annual return, Article 13(8)`
    `the entries to be made on the register in respect of the annual return, Article 13(8)`
    `the details of payments to a governor that an annual return must include, Article 13(9)(a)`
    `the statement of current intentions as to payments to a governor, Article 13(9)(b)`
    `the entry on the register of those details and of that statement, Article 13(9)(c)`
    `relief for a prescribed description of charity, Article 13(10)`

DECLARE `Approval or permission of the Commissioner under Article 13` IS ONE OF
    `approval of a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)(b)`
    `approval of a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)`
    `prior permission to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition, Article 13(5)(b)`
    `permission to amend the statement of intentions as to payments, Article 13(11)(b)`

-- 13(6): the eight kinds of matter.  Each constructor carries the facts its own paragraph turns on, as a witness could state them.
-- Only (e) names a governor (by the name entered in the `Governor` record of the entity).
DECLARE `Matter to report under Article 13(6)` IS ONE OF
    `a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register`
        HAS `information about the matter is entered on the register in relation to the charity` IS A BOOLEAN
            `the matter has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a matter coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name`
        HAS `the matter came to light after registration or after permission for a change of name` IS A BOOLEAN
            `the matter could, if known before, have led the Commissioner to refuse to register the charity` IS A BOOLEAN
            `the matter could, if known before, have led the Commissioner to enter the charity in a different section` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a proposal to change the charity's constitution`
        HAS `there is a proposal to change the charity's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a proposal or an event affecting the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)`
        HAS `there is a proposal that could result in the charity ceasing to meet those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
            `an event has occurred that has resulted in the charity ceasing to meet those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reportable matter in relation to a governor`
        HAS `governor's name` IS A STRING
            `the charity is aware that the governor has not promptly reported the matter to the Commissioner under Article 19(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a matter likely to lead to bankruptcy, winding up or ceasing to exist`
        HAS `the matter is likely to lead to the charity becoming bankrupt, being wound up or otherwise ceasing to exist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets its restricted-section condition`
        HAS `there is a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets a condition prescribed under Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a matter prescribed by Order under Article 13(6)(h)`
        HAS `the matter is within a description prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN

-- When the event or proposal happened and when the charity became aware of it: the two anchors of "promptly" (fork F5.1) and of "arising
-- during the year" (fork F5.13).
DECLARE `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` HAS
    `date of the event or proposal` IS A DATE @desc The day the event happened or the proposal was made
    `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS A DATE @desc The day the charity became aware of the matter

-- What was done about the matter: the report.
DECLARE `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` HAS
    `date the report was made` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if no report has been made to the Commissioner
    `the report was made promptly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The judgement that the report was prompt; read only on the reading of fork F5.1 that takes promptness as an input

-- A statement of current intentions as to payments (Article 13(9)(b)), as provided to the Commissioner on a day.  Whether a given payment is
-- inconsistent with it is a judgement (an input), asked of each statement the charity has provided.
DECLARE `Statement of intentions as to payments` HAS
    `date provided` IS A DATE @desc The day the charity provided the statement to the Commissioner (or the day an amended statement took the place of an earlier one)
    `the payment is inconsistent with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The judgement that the payment in question is inconsistent with this statement

DECLARE `Payment by the charity` HAS
    description IS A STRING @desc The payment, in words
    `date of the payment` IS A DATE @desc The day the payment was made
    `statements provided` IS A LIST OF `Statement of intentions as to payments` @desc Every statement of current intentions the charity has provided under an Order under Article 13(9)(b), the amended ones included, with whether this payment is inconsistent with each

DECLARE `Act under Article 13` IS ONE OF
    `provide public benefit in accordance with the registered public benefit statement`
        HAS statement IS A STRING
    `provide evidence of a reason justifying the request, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner`
    `ensure that the charity meets the condition on which it is entered in the restricted section`
    `report a matter to the Commissioner`
        HAS matter IS A `Matter to report under Article 13(6)`
    `send the annual return to the Commissioner`
    `make a payment`
        HAS payment IS A `Payment by the charity`
    `apply to the Commissioner for permission to amend the statement of intentions`
        HAS reasons IS A STRING
    `provide the Commissioner with a statement of current intentions as to payments to a governor`
    `make an Order`
        HAS subject IS A `Subject of an Order under Article 13`
    `make Regulations requiring a charity or its governors to avoid, or report and remedy, a later ground for refusal`
    `give an approval or permission`
        HAS about IS AN `Approval or permission of the Commissioner under Article 13`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13(2) and 13(3): a provision of the constitution or constitutional Law about amending the purposes.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Provision about amending purposes` HAS
    `forms part of the entity's constitution or constitutional Law` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the provision is a provision of the entity's constitution (Article 2(4)) or of its constitutional Law (Article 2(5)); where Article 2(5) names no constitutional Law for this kind of entity, only a provision of the constitution can be one
    `purports to permit an amendment to include any purpose whatever` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE for a provision that does not restrict the purposes an amendment may add or substitute
    `purposes whose addition or substitution it purports to permit` IS A LIST OF Purpose
        @desc The purposes that a restricted provision purports to allow an amendment to add or substitute; empty for an unrestricted provision
    `an order of the court under the Loi of 1862 exists, made before or after registration` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 13(13): an order of the court under the Loi of 1862 affecting the provision, made before or after the charity was registered
    `that order is inconsistent with paragraph (2) or (3) as applied to the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 13(13): the order is inconsistent with Article 13(2) or (3) as those would apply to the provision

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13(5): the condition of the restricted section.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Facts about the condition of the restricted section` HAS
    `meets the condition as to which the Commissioner was satisfied under Article 9(6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the charity meets the condition, prescribed under Article 9(2), on which it was entered in the restricted section
    `ceased to meet that condition` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the charity has ceased to meet that condition
    `the Commissioner gave permission to remain entered on the basis of a different condition` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the Commissioner gave a permission of the kind Article 13(5)(b) describes
    `that permission was given before the charity ceased to meet the original condition` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the permission was prior to the cessation; FALSE if there is no permission
    `meets the different condition as specified in the permission` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the charity meets the different condition, as the permission specifies it

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13(7), 13(8): the annual return.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The day on which a financial year ends, for the reading of fork F5.2 that takes the year of the return to be the charity's financial year.
DECLARE `Day on which a financial year ends` HAS
    month IS A NUMBER @desc Month, 1 to 12
    day IS A NUMBER @desc Day of the month, 1 to 31

DECLARE `Year to which an annual return relates` HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Matter arising for the annual return` HAS
    reference IS A STRING @desc A name for the matter
    `falls within paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter falls within one of the paragraphs (a) to (h) of Article 13(6)
    timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)`
    `the annual return gives information about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the return contains information about the matter

-- What an Order under Article 13(7) and (8) provides.  None is in the sources: the caller supplies the Order, or NOTHING.
DECLARE `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` HAS
    `due date of the annual return` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if the Order sets no date
    `consequence of lateness` IS A MAYBE STRING @desc NOTHING if the Order states no consequence; otherwise the consequence in words

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13(10): relief for small charities.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Provision that an Order under Article 13(10) may relieve` IS ONE OF
    `a provision of paragraph (6)`
    `a provision of paragraph (7)`
    `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7)`
    `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)`
    `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)`

-- The provision actually in question, as distinguished from the provision an Order names: the Law has no Order under paragraph (8), but an Order
-- under paragraph (7) may contain provision made by virtue of paragraph (8) (format, timing, lateness, register entries).
DECLARE `Provision in question under Article 13(10)` IS ONE OF
    `a provision of paragraph (6)`
    `a provision of paragraph (7)`
    `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) not made by virtue of paragraph (8)`
    `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)`
    `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)`

DECLARE `Effect of an Order under Article 13(10) on a provision` IS ONE OF
    `the provision applies in full`
    `the provision does not apply to the charity`
    `the provision applies to the charity only subject to a modification`
        HAS modification IS A STRING @desc The modification the Order prescribes

DECLARE `Relief given by an Order under Article 13(10)` IS ONE OF
    `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)`
    `relief by modification, Article 13(10)(b)`
        HAS modification IS A STRING @desc The modification the Order prescribes

DECLARE `Order under Article 13(10)` HAS
    provision IS A `Provision that an Order under Article 13(10) may relieve`
    relief IS A `Relief given by an Order under Article 13(10)`
    `the Minister consulted the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 13(10)(a); for relief by modification, the corresponding opinion in 13(10)(b) that the modification gives reasonable relief having regard to those matters
    `the charity is of the prescribed description` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13(9): an Order requiring payment details and a statement of intentions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Order under Article 13(9)` HAS
    `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Payment to a governor or a connected person` HAS
    description IS A STRING @desc The payment, in words
    `date of the payment` IS A DATE @desc The day the payment was made
    `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made to a governor of the charity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment is of the description the Order under Article 13(9)(a) prescribes
    `the annual return gives its details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the annual return includes the details of the payment

§§ `Part 4 -- Charity register: nouns of Article 14 (Powers of court over registered charity)`

-- Who applies to the court.  Article 14(1) allows two, Article 14(4) four; a fifth kind (anyone else) is allowed by neither.
-- (The constructors are named for the application so that they do not collide with the constructors of `Legal actor` in domain.l4.)
DECLARE `Application to the court under Article 14` IS ONE OF
    `an application by the Commissioner`
    `an application by the Attorney General`
    `an application by the registered charity`
    `an application by a person to whom the order was directed`
    `an application by any other person`

-- Who an order is directed at.  Article 14(3) names the persons for whom an order of that kind is possible.
DECLARE `Person at whom an order is directed` IS ONE OF
    `the charity`
    `a governor of the charity`
    `another person concerned in the management or control of the charity`
    `a person who holds property on behalf of the charity`
    `a person who holds property on behalf of a governor of the charity`
    `another person who appears to be responsible for misconduct`
    `any other person`
    `no person in particular`

-- Article 14(3)(a)(i) to (iii): what a prohibiting order forbids.
DECLARE `Action that an order under Article 14(3)(a) forbids` IS ONE OF
    `referring to or holding out the entity as a charity or Jersey charity, or as being charitable, having charitable purposes or providing public benefit`
    `soliciting donations from the public, as specified in the order`
    `taking any other action specified in the order`

-- "whether for a specified or indefinite period" (14(3)(a), (b)); "from such time, and for such periods" (14(3)(g)).
DECLARE `Period of an order of the court` IS ONE OF
    `an indefinite period`
        HAS `first day named` IS A DATE @desc The first day the order names for its operation; the order then runs until it is amended or revoked
    `a specified period`
        HAS `first day named` IS A DATE @desc The first day the order names for its operation
            `number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the period in days

-- The order the court is asked to make under Article 14(3).
DECLARE `Order proposed under Article 14(3)` HAS
    kind IS AN `Order of the court over a charity` @desc Which of the nine listed kinds of order (Article 14(3)(a) to (i))
    `directed at` IS A `Person at whom an order is directed`
    forbids IS A MAYBE `Action that an order under Article 14(3)(a) forbids` @desc For an order under (a), what it forbids; NOTHING for any other kind
    `it appears to the court that the person at whom the order is directed has engaged in misconduct or is responsible for it` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 14(3)(h): a governor who appears to the court to have engaged in any misconduct, or another person who appears to be responsible for it
    period IS A `Period of an order of the court`

-- What appears to the court when it is asked to exercise the powers (Article 14(1)): the facts are given as they appear to the court.
DECLARE `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` HAS
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the conduct bears on the administration of the charity
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary meaning of the word, apart from Article 2(10)
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 14(1)(b): necessary or desirable for protecting the property of the charity or securing a proper application of that property in accordance with the charity's registered charitable purposes and registered public benefit statement

-- What the court sees fit under Article 14(2).
DECLARE `Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` HAS
    `to remedy the misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to protect the property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to secure its proper application` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Act under Article 14` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the court`
        HAS application IS AN `Application to the court under Article 14`
    `exercise the powers set out in Article 14(2)`
    `make an order that the court sees fit`
    `make an order of a kind listed in Article 14(3)`
        HAS kind IS AN `Order of the court over a charity`
    `amend or revoke an order made under Article 14`
